# {{ if .DisplayName }}{{ .DisplayName }}{{ else }}{{ .Container }}{{ end }}

The `{{ .Container }}` function of {{ .SoftwareSystem }}, in project {{ .Project }}: an AWS
Lambda function in Go, on the AWS SDK for Go v2, behind an API Gateway HTTP
API, keeping items in a DynamoDB table, with its infrastructure as a CDK app. Scaffolded by C4
Factory.

## The API

Every request is signed with AWS credentials (SigV4): the API's routes use IAM
authorization, and a caller needs `execute-api:Invoke` on them.

| Route             | Body                                | Answers                                    |
| ----------------- | ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| `PUT /items/{id}` | `{ "name": "Lamp", "quantity": 3 }` | 200 and the item; 400 for a bad id or body |
| `GET /items/{id}` |                                     | 200 and the item; 404 when there is none   |

An id is 1 to 64 letters, digits, `-` or `_`. A name is 1 to 200 characters;
a quantity a whole number, 0 or more. Every error is JSON with a `message`.
A `PUT` replaces the whole item, so repeating it is harmless.

## Develop

Open the repository in its devcontainer, which has Go 1.26 and Node 24.

```sh
npm ci                     # install the CDK app's exact packages
(cd src && go test ./...)  # the function's tests
npm test                   # the stacks' assertions, with vitest
npm run synth              # build the function, write the templates into cdk.out/
{{- if .Standard }}
make check                 # what CI runs: format, lint, vet, test, synth, cfn-lint
make help                  # every target
{{- end }}
```

Nothing here deploys or needs an AWS account: synth runs offline, builds the
function with the installed Go, and needs neither Docker nor credentials.
Deploying the stack (`cdk deploy`, after `cdk bootstrap` of the account) is
for its owner, with their own credentials.

## Layout

- `src/` is the function, a Go module of its own (`src/go.mod`). `main.go`
  is the Lambda entry point: it loads the AWS configuration and creates the
  DynamoDB client once, reads `TABLE_NAME` and hands each request to
  `answer` in `api.go`.
- `api.go` routes a request, checks its input and answers with a status
  code; `items.go` holds the rules, free of AWS; `item_store.go` keeps items
  in DynamoDB behind the `ItemStore` interface tests fake.
- `infra/stacks.ts` defines the stacks; `infra/api_stack.ts` is the one
  stack: the table, the function, built by `go build` into one `bootstrap`
  binary for arm64, with its log group and role, and the API with its access
  log. The stack is named after the package.
{{- if .Standard }}
- `infra/main.ts` is the CDK app `cdk synth` runs (`cdk.json`), and
  `infra/standard.ts` tags every stack and adds CDK Nag's checks.

Read `AGENTS.md` before changing anything: it is the rulebook, for people and agents.
{{- end }}
